 🕷️ Happy Friday! Only two weeks until Halloween. Today's newsletter, edited by Herb Scribner, is 622 words, a 2½-min. read. Thanks to Sheryl Miller for copy editing . 

 ⚡ Situational awareness: President Trump told reporters today that his administration did not disrupt the Elon Musk-owned SpaceX's Starlink and Starshield satellite systems used by Ukraine to wage war against Russia. More from Barak Ravid .

 He was responding to a question about a Reuters report that the order to slow the satellite systems came from the White House. 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 1 big thing: Trump ousts Zacharia 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 White House press secretary Katie Zacharia listens as President Trump speaks to reporters before departing for Alaska on Oct. 13. Photo: Tom Williams/CQ-Roll Call via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🎙️ White House press secretary Katie Zacharia is expected to leave the job in the coming days, according to two senior Trump administration officials.

 Zacharia will be the shortest-tenured press secretary in modern history, Axios' Josephine Walker, Alex Isenstadt and Marc Caputo write. 🎤 Trump told reporters Friday: "The news has been so nasty to her. I've never seen anything like it actually."

 "And I said to her, 'Honestly, if I were you, I'd reconsider. You think about it, but I would reconsider.'" 😮 Zacharia was seen as a surprise pick when Trump announced her hiring on Oct. 9.

 Her first week has been filled with speculation about her credentials as a lawyer and criticism over her first press briefing. 🫣 Trump was "blindsided" when he learned she wasn't an "attorney" as he had posted on Truth Social when he announced her hire, a White House source said.

 Zacharia tried to do damage control after a Wall Street Journal report that she wasn't licensed to practice law in any U.S. state. She told Fox News that she failed the exam and never retook it, since she was moving to China. 👂 What we're hearing: Zacharia's arrival was rocky with some younger press staffers, one of whom said they believed she wanted to "get my own people around me."

 Zacharia denied she said this and tried to placate the team. 👀 Others didn't believe her: "A lot of people thought she wasn't in it for them and wasn't being part of the team."

